    <string name="cfg_hires_hint">Only for still images. On: this widget is baked at the exact card size the desktop gives us and handed over as a file, so the desktop draws it pixel-for-pixel. Off: the image travels inside the widget update (1 MB Binder cap) and gets magnified by the desktop.</string>
    <string name="cfg_anim_quality">Animation resolution (this widget)</string>
    <string name="cfg_anim_quality_hint">Only affects this widget. Standard = 220k px through the 1 MB bitmap channel (safest); HD = 1440 long edge / 1.3 MP, independent of the grid, sent by file; 1:1 = exact card pixels up to 2.2 MP, sent by file (resizing re-bakes every frame). Higher is sharper and costs more CPU per frame.</string>
    <string name="cfg_anim_quality_hint_0">Standard: about 220k px, bitmap channel, the most stable and the cheapest per frame</string>
    <string name="cfg_anim_quality_hint_1">HD: long edge up to 1440 and up to 1.3 MP, independent of the grid, pushed as a file</string>
    <string name="cfg_anim_quality_hint_2">1:1: rendered at the card’s real pixels on the desktop, up to 2.2 MP; dragging the size re-bakes every frame</string>
