    <string name="cfg_notes">"Tips:
• The shape mask fills the selected layout area; the rest is transparent. With shadow on, the mask leaves a small inset for the shadow.
• Scale 100 = fill the layout; lower values shrink content, mask, border and shadow together.
• Star / heart / eye / crescent and the other shapes with their own proportions are scaled uniformly and centered (never squashed); box-like shapes (rect, rounded, ellipse, capsule, hexagon…) still fill the layout.
• Images have one frame; video/GIF are sampled at the chosen rate.
• GIF / images in the smooth overlay support layout, scale, rotation, border and shadow; video overlay stays a rectangle.
• Higher resolution/quality uses more storage and battery.
• Frame pushing depends on the system and launcher; the real frame rate may be lower than set."</string>
