    <string name="settings_nocanvas_hint">On (recommended): frames are prepared once at the source aspect, so resizing never redoes them and nothing stutters. Off: frames match the exact grid pixels — sharpest, but every resize redoes the whole batch (slow)</string>
    <string name="settings_hires_static">1:1 HD for still images (default for new widgets)</string>
    <string name="settings_hires_static_hint">Only the default for widgets you add from now on — each widget can override it in its own editor. On: still images are prepared at the real on-screen size, so the launcher no longer upscales them</string>
    <string name="settings_anim_quality">Animated quality (default for new widgets)</string>
    <string name="settings_anim_quality_hint">Only the default for new widgets — each widget can override it in its own editor. Sharper costs more: Standard (safest) → HD → 1:1 (sharpest, resizing redoes every frame)</string>
    <string name="settings_anim_quality_hint_0">Standard: about 220k px, bitmap channel (most stable)</string>
    <string name="settings_anim_quality_hint_1">HD: long edge up to 1440, up to 1.3M px, pushed as a file</string>
    <string name="settings_anim_quality_hint_2">1:1: rendered at the card’s real pixels (up to 2.2M px); resizing re-bakes every frame</string>
